            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0578" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.9169/4120d: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-16T15:00:00-04:00">June 16, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1206. Your 1856 of May 24, 1591 of May 5, and 1352 of April 19. Department and
                    FEA are gratified that the Swedes have taken steps to end shipment of coal to
                    Norway via Bothnian route. However, we still wish to obtain if possible the
                    limitations requested in your <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of May 5
                    (your 1591 and 1352). Please continue to make every effort to achieve our
                    objective at an early date. The procedure <pb facs="0579" n="569" xml:id="pg569"
                    /> to be used is left to your discretion. This telegram is being repeated to
                    London and the British Embassy here is telegraphing London so that your British
                    colleague will receive parallel instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
